%% 2026-04-10 extension for predict_interview_qa
%% New additive outputs: company_dossier, interview_risk_map, confidence_breakdown, reliability_state.
%% The existing three-tab UI and SQLite-backed prediction table remain unchanged.
%% Lightweight crawl stays same-domain first, with safe caps and no JS/PDF default.
%% The Interview Q&A detail view renders company_dossier and interview_risk_map from normalized payloads when available.
%% Prediction rows expose Recall/Edit, which reloads stored input snapshot data when available so operators can edit and rerun a prior submission.
%% Automation run logs are created early, and log viewer fallback uses stored run detail when the file path is stale.
%% Interview crawl canonicalizes www/non-www same-domain matching to keep redirecting company sites in the same coverage bucket.
%% Generation prompt carries dossier summaries plus page titles and URLs to strengthen company understanding when multiple public pages are available.
%% 2026-04-11 update: date-triggered pending runs and schedule overrides now use a short misfire grace window so minor sync delay does not drop queued runs.
%% 2026-04-11 update: predict_interview_qa now defaults to a shorter LLM timeout so unresponsive local model calls fail fast and fall back sooner.
%% 2026-04-11 update: predict_interview_qa now synthesizes a grounded heuristic payload on model timeout so the run can complete without a second blocking vet call.
%% 2026-04-11 update: the generation prompt is compacted to reduce token pressure and lower Ollama latency in the hot path.
%% 2026-04-11 update: predict_interview_qa now uses a 20-second model timeout with no retry loop so fallback activates quickly instead of compounding latency.
%% 2026-04-11 update: predict_interview_qa now separates intent and proof bundles before generation so the final pack keeps one interview angle per question when possible.
%% 2026-04-11 update: a rule-based dedup pass drops repeated answer skeletons and moves low-uniqueness questions into gap/drill items instead of persisting template-like duplicates.
%% 2026-04-12 update: Reposts Analytics now includes Stack Trends, which classifies jobs into stack groups and surfaces crawl recommendations for thin buckets.
%% 2026-04-12 update: Stack Trends reuses the same cached external source pattern as Language Trends so broader world context stays off the hot path.
%% 2026-04-12 update: stale external market context now returns cached data immediately and refreshes in the background instead of blocking the analytics chart.
%% 2026-04-12 update: trend AI snapshots are now refreshed nightly and persisted to SQLite so page load only reads the DB snapshot.
%% 2026-04-12 update: automation completion profiles are incrementally updated from run logs and the Runs table reads ETA from SQLite snapshots.
%% 2026-04-12 update: the schedules table now defaults to next_run_at ascending so operators see the nearest upcoming execution first.
%% 2026-04-12 update: schedules now reuse completion profiles to estimate next-run duration and end time, and the form warns about likely overlap windows before save.
%% 2026-04-12 update: the frontend shell now reads the shared full i18n map from AppRuntime so automation labels do not disappear after page splits.
%% 2026-04-12 update: the Automation schedules table CSS now matches the 9 rendered columns so name and action cells no longer collapse from stale nth-child mappings.
%% 2026-04-14 update: LinkedIn public job HTML parsing now stores public_apply_mode=onsite/offsite from topbar apply markers, and easy_apply normalization/filtering treats onsite as Easy Apply.
%% 2026-04-14 update: /api/jobs easy_apply filtering also falls back to payload apply_url markers (linkedin.com, onsiteapply, easyapply) so historical rows without normalized_easy_apply backfill still stay visible.
%% 2026-04-14 update: a lightweight requests-first easy_apply_probe backfills recent jobs outside the /api/jobs hot path, with browser probing kept only as fallback.
%% 2026-04-14 update: Easy Apply buttons remain available on Easy-Apply rows without pre-rendered CV files because backend apply can auto-generate uploadable CV artifacts on demand.
%% 2026-04-14 update: LinkedIn apply runtime now retries Playwright launch without the extension when extension startup closes early, and failed env-cookie auth clears cookies before login probing.
%% 2026-04-14 update: Multi-job LinkedIn apply preserves requested job_ids order when pairing jobs with cv_paths, preventing silent CV/job mismatches in batch runs.
%% 2026-04-14 update: LinkedIn apply logging now records per-job CV resolution fallback, parsed statuses, diagnostics, and trace-log paths for easier post-run review.
%% 2026-04-14 update: questionnaire-context now includes similar_answer_memory collected from recent apply_field_input/change logs and injects it into llm_prompt_template.
%% 2026-04-14 update: POST /api/linkedin/apply/questionnaire-draft/{job_id} now returns structured LLM answer drafts for operator review without changing final-submit safeguards.
%% 2026-04-14 update: CV preview materialized-state now requires binary artifact paths (.pdf/.docx); TXT-only CV and cover-letter paths map to artifact_text.
%% 2026-04-14 update: CV preview logs include explicit state-resolution diagnostics with binary-path candidates to speed up apply-run troubleshooting.
%% 2026-04-14 update: LinkedIn Apply Logger now captures compact field answer values and richer field context for apply_field_input/change so similar-answer memory has reusable evidence.
%% 2026-04-14 update: Logger input capture is scoped to Easy Apply flow with throttling, and popup now shows sync health metadata (pending count, last sync, last error).
%% 2026-04-14 update: Added nightly closed_jobs_check pipeline and check_no_longer_accepting_jobs action with checkpoint windows (first run 10 days; subsequent runs 5 recent + 5 anchored from previous check date).
%% 2026-04-14 update: Closed-marker hits are now auto-marked as priority_flag=closed_no_longer_accepting via job_application_tracking instead of immediate hard-delete.
%% 2026-04-17 update: Added automate_easy_apply schedule pipeline that applies to a capped set of Easy Apply jobs nightly and persists applied_label=Automate Easy apply.
